#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096379 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b8f8937b-de15-5d4c-aa77-1d45595fc7af" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations Using Back Substitution"}] :question/id #uuid "201a713a-83ca-5e31-9a4f-257795d7eb1b" :question/math-academy-id "e-4690" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y+z=3 \\\\ y+z=2 \\\\ z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The third equation states that $z=2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+(2)=2 \n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\ty = 2-2 = 0.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute both $z=2$ and $y=0$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+(0)+(2)=3\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx = 3-2 = 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x = 1,$ $y=0,$ and $z = 2.$ Or, in vector form, the solution is $\\langle 1,0,2 \\rangle.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096380 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de05090a-2461-514a-971d-b83c7cea124e" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations Using Back Substitution Given an Augmented Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "cc8ce97a-3bda-506f-b9d2-98ac7524583a" :question/math-academy-id "e-4691" :question/problem "Solve the system of equations that is represented by the augmented matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x_1,$ $x_2,$ and $x_3.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-2 \\\\ {x}_{3}=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that $x_3=5.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_2+(5)=-2\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx_2=-2-5=-7.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute both $x_3 = 5$ and $x_2 = -7$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx_1+(-7)-(5) = 1\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx_1 = 1 + 7 + 5 = 13.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x_1 = 13,$ $x_2=-7,$ and $x_3 = 5.$ Or, in vector form, the solution is $\\langle 13,-7,5 \\rangle.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096381 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "52e51c9a-6bce-5ea6-a9fe-febb09f8754d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations Given an Augmented Matrix Containing Non-Unit Leading Entries"}] :question/id #uuid "7b44089c-8ca7-57e5-b390-7900647e3884" :question/math-academy-id "e-4692" :question/problem "Solve the system of equations that is represented by the augmented matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 3\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x_1,$ $x_2,$ and $x_3.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-2 \\\\ 3{x}_{3}=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that\n\n$$\n3x_3=3 \n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad \n\tx_3=1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_2+(1)=-2\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx_2=-2-1=-3.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute both $x_3 = 1$ and $x_2 = -3$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n2x_1+(-3)-(1) = 0\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx_1 = \\dfrac{1}{2} (3 + 1) = 2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x_1 = 2,$ $x_2=-3,$ and $x_3 = 1.$ Or, in vector form, the solution is $\\langle 2,-3,1 \\rangle.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304918 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b8f8937b-de15-5d4c-aa77-1d45595fc7af" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations Using Back Substitution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc0a6eba-eb8b-58ec-8897-d0cf1febfe20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{1}{2},-1,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304920} {:answer/id #uuid "ae09bc59-42cc-51aa-9db6-d093d23069fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3}{2},1,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304921} {:answer/id #uuid "bdfacfc6-c10d-5ce5-8763-0b7178d5f4fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{3}{2},-1,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304922} {:answer/id #uuid "6f792197-a7a6-50d1-9961-b194c7b83e98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{2},-1,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304923} {:answer/id #uuid "90eec126-71d1-5c9a-9cb6-21f58fa00483" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{3}{2},1,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304924}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc0a6eba-eb8b-58ec-8897-d0cf1febfe20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{1}{2},-1,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304920} :answer-field/id #uuid "be15f084-0468-539e-9586-3dcf21de9144" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304919}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "86f396e6-bece-557c-89fe-7bc8d07b01b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-10195" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+y+z=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & y+z=1 \\\\  & z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The third equation states that  $z=2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get \n\n$$\ny+2=1\\,⟹\\,y=1-2=-1.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=2$ and $y=-1$into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+(-1)+(2)=\\frac{1}{2}\\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{1}{2}-2+1=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-\\frac{1}{2}$, $y=-1$, and $z=2.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨-\\frac{1}{2},-1,2⟩.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304925 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b8f8937b-de15-5d4c-aa77-1d45595fc7af" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations Using Back Substitution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64e1c4fa-7964-539e-ba2f-0cbc349382a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5,2,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304927} {:answer/id #uuid "368b36f4-17b6-51cf-a950-0dc99d21e7a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨7,3,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304928} {:answer/id #uuid "0f772a7f-048a-537d-a117-892b331c647e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5,3,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304929} {:answer/id #uuid "95b97466-613f-5dad-a9cc-1df6ee9e20ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨7,-2,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304930} {:answer/id #uuid "4d92fa0b-61ff-5cf6-b0a7-2b60b6c5a15f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6,2,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304931}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "368b36f4-17b6-51cf-a950-0dc99d21e7a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨7,3,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304928} :answer-field/id #uuid "cdb603b5-cfa3-51c1-a64d-0eaea53c68f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304926}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "557245ad-45e9-56b6-9e4b-33daba094cce" :question/math-academy-id "q-10199" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-y-z=3 \\\\  & y-z=2 \\\\  & z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The third equation states that $z=1.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny-(1)=2\\,⟹\\,y=2+1=3.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=1$ and $y=3$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx-(3)-(1)=3\\,⟹\\,x=3+4=7.\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=7$,  $y=3$,  and $z=1.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨7,3,1⟩.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304932 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "52e51c9a-6bce-5ea6-a9fe-febb09f8754d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations Given an Augmented Matrix Containing Non-Unit Leading Entries"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa53efee-83ce-5308-9161-139ad9390047" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,-1,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304934} {:answer/id #uuid "aa116539-a226-5200-9cb2-c11a3659577b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,-2,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304935} {:answer/id #uuid "4d4d3fa8-869f-5a4f-b976-dfd62a77f30d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,1,-8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304936} {:answer/id #uuid "cbf4b6b5-bc24-5f6d-b9f5-7ecf4966ace1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,-1,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304937} {:answer/id #uuid "848de5e7-387e-5d76-a00a-a3a0e44658d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-1,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304938}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa53efee-83ce-5308-9161-139ad9390047" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,-1,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304934} :answer-field/id #uuid "63515660-8cda-56ff-ae25-8ef09026bdd0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304933}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c7e4218f-47e8-518f-8a12-cc5cea874766" :question/math-academy-id "q-10203" :question/problem "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x$, $y$, and $z.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 2x-2y+z=8 \\\\  & y-z=-1 \\\\  & z=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that $z=0.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny-0=-1\\,⟹\\,y=-1.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=0$ and $y=-1$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n2x-2(-1)+(0)=8\\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{8-2}{2}=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=3$, $y=-1$, and $z=0.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨3,-1,0⟩.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096843 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "52e51c9a-6bce-5ea6-a9fe-febb09f8754d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations Given an Augmented Matrix Containing Non-Unit Leading Entries"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bea848db-ef9a-541f-ae21-65420fcba9a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨ - 75,-10,-5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093466} {:answer/id #uuid "eea79d80-0e7f-54ea-a83d-ebf24abae586" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨ - 85, 40,-5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093467} {:answer/id #uuid "15a62892-6d88-55a9-b52b-979ee77bc897" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨ - 5,-10, 5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093468} {:answer/id #uuid "20f95d48-197f-5df0-a7ae-9aeb8878fd0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨ - 15, 40,-5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093469} {:answer/id #uuid "4410fd43-4572-5645-8e43-0e582aa6a5c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨ - 75, 40,-5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093470}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4410fd43-4572-5645-8e43-0e582aa6a5c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨ - 75, 40,-5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093470} :answer-field/id #uuid "9de6dddc-90d9-53d0-a997-faa7291342ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093465}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5592cf72-9e61-50b5-9aec-b1921100f3dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-10204" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+2y-z=10 \\\\  & y+5z=15 \\\\  & -z=5\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The third equation states that \n\n$$\n-z=5\\,⟹\\,z=-5.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+5(-5)=15\\,⟹\\,y=15+25=40.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=-5$ and $y=40$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+2(40)-(-5)=10\\,⟹\\,x=10-80-5=-75.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-75,y=40$ and $z=-5.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨-75,40,-5⟩.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304939 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b8f8937b-de15-5d4c-aa77-1d45595fc7af" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations Using Back Substitution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd5346a4-ea23-5594-8312-c9e8aea44d71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304941} {:answer/id #uuid "a31375a6-883e-5051-a742-29eedb120fc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{15}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304942} {:answer/id #uuid "3d476a05-b478-5bef-89be-a3483c85ae39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304943} {:answer/id #uuid "3a955797-f60a-5584-919d-01520baa4d35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{15}{2} \\\\ \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304944} {:answer/id #uuid "71d7d0c6-68a9-5712-891a-739df23e3015" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ \\frac{7}{2} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304945}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "71d7d0c6-68a9-5712-891a-739df23e3015" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ \\frac{7}{2} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304945} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f80d039-b214-5111-9821-e8630f15c48e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304940}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8a0e4715-4168-526b-b47f-345c81075134" :question/math-academy-id "q-129452" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+y-z=2 \\\\  & y-z=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & z=3\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The third equation states that $z=3.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny-3=\\frac{1}{2}\\,⟹\\,y=\\frac{1}{2}+3=\\frac{7}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $y=\\frac{7}{2}$ and $z=3$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+\\frac{7}{2}-3=2\\,⟹\\,x=2-\\frac{7}{2}+3=\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=\\frac{3}{2}$, $y=\\frac{7}{2}$, and $z=3.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as\n$[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ \\frac{7}{2} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304946 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b8f8937b-de15-5d4c-aa77-1d45595fc7af" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations Using Back Substitution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c962ceb6-409c-5124-afc2-a6d64148752d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6,4,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304948} {:answer/id #uuid "4b84e5c0-3561-52ba-93cc-3f1a680e649c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,0,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304949} {:answer/id #uuid "0f5b96bc-def3-5c89-9a75-2217f73e12ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-4,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304950} {:answer/id #uuid "11bf684e-b138-555b-a78c-c8a467bbe757" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6,0,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304951} {:answer/id #uuid "6f35bf38-5dec-5af3-864d-a8ac611887a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6,-4,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304952}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c962ceb6-409c-5124-afc2-a6d64148752d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6,4,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304948} :answer-field/id #uuid "16b5d9ec-a320-5176-8d70-cce6444eb15e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304947}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "aa040e85-cfaf-56bd-b394-34ac6e069fef" :question/math-academy-id "q-129453" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=4 \\\\  & {x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=2 \\\\  & {x}_{3}=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The third equation states that ${x}_{3}=-2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+(-2)=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=2+2=4.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{2}=4$ and ${x}_{3}=-2$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-4-(-2)=4\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=4+4-2=6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is ${x}_{1}=6$, ${x}_{2}=4$, and ${x}_{3}=-2.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨6,4,-2⟩.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304953 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de05090a-2461-514a-971d-b83c7cea124e" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations Using Back Substitution Given an Augmented Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28a64c07-1e37-5008-9614-b71485ada7a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,12,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304955} {:answer/id #uuid "18fae80b-6dea-5c12-a1af-d72bc7e5108c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,-12,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304956} {:answer/id #uuid "264949a0-af89-584e-9adf-a8be61d6a1f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,-12,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304957} {:answer/id #uuid "48f920e7-68eb-5ca2-8d90-52212ac5ae19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-22,12,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304958} {:answer/id #uuid "467732f5-8683-5df6-8520-cc82d38631c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-22,-12,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304959}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "264949a0-af89-584e-9adf-a8be61d6a1f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,-12,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304957} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f63b891-747a-5381-97f9-79b498dc5190" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304954}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e303c953-d83b-5fd3-b1b2-48ffdf768a6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-129459" :question/problem "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x$, $y$, and $z.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+y+3z=-2 \\\\  & y+4z=0 \\\\  & z=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that $z=3.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+4(3)=0\\,⟹\\,y=-12.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=3$ and $y=-12$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+(-12)+3(3)=-2\\,⟹\\,x=-2+12-9=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=1$, $y=-12$, and $z=3.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨1,-12,3⟩.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304960 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de05090a-2461-514a-971d-b83c7cea124e" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations Using Back Substitution Given an Augmented Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b857276e-b1e0-5673-8dc3-023d455f1e71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨7,-4,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304962} {:answer/id #uuid "99568179-759a-5036-8a90-de1cae6320db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨7,2,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304963} {:answer/id #uuid "94d8d6a9-37b5-5d9c-b143-db45dda31501" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨11,2,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304964} {:answer/id #uuid "31d3929d-40e1-5c75-a958-1a6f8b5f4cfc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-5,-4,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304965} {:answer/id #uuid "547c829e-2139-5580-ba1b-56c8e0f8a4ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨11,4,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304966}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "547c829e-2139-5580-ba1b-56c8e0f8a4ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨11,4,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304966} :answer-field/id #uuid "32714145-cff6-5187-a015-f39d08c18b4a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304961}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0eaa730f-d0fe-50bd-974e-f7fe25ee9ac0" :question/math-academy-id "q-129569" :question/problem "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say,  ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & {x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\  & {x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=3 \\\\  & {x}_{3}=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that ${x}_{3}=-1.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+(-1)=3\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=3+1=4.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{3}=-1$ and ${x}_{2}=4$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-2(4)+3(-1)=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=8+3=11.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is ${x}_{1}=11$, ${x}_{2}=4$, and ${x}_{3}=-1.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨11,4,-1⟩.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304967 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de05090a-2461-514a-971d-b83c7cea124e" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations Using Back Substitution Given an Augmented Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4dad004-aa19-56f3-89ea-60e4cd24d8b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-7,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304969} {:answer/id #uuid "f037ea77-52d5-56a3-931c-215f425627df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,7,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304970} {:answer/id #uuid "d3dd163c-b4e2-5d8c-8be9-72d600368503" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-14,-7,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304971} {:answer/id #uuid "a5be4491-5bf5-56aa-a1ee-6a4e20e5df53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-14,7,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304972} {:answer/id #uuid "77a84be8-010b-5f74-b393-7b42bc5eb19d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,-11,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304973}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4dad004-aa19-56f3-89ea-60e4cd24d8b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-7,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304969} :answer-field/id #uuid "51eed673-092b-5fe8-a63b-005d40d6f5d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304968}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c9c569ea-99ad-5869-84a0-439292a9f3cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-129599" :question/problem "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x$, $y$, and $z.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+y+2z=-1 \\\\  & y+3z=2 \\\\  & z=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that $z=3.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+3(3)=2\\,⟹\\,y=2-9=-7.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=3$ and $y=-7$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+(-7)+2(3)=-1\\,⟹\\,x=-1+7-6=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=0$, $y=-7$, and $z=3.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨0,-7,3⟩.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304974 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "52e51c9a-6bce-5ea6-a9fe-febb09f8754d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations Given an Augmented Matrix Containing Non-Unit Leading Entries"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dd95bf8e-829a-55b9-89e9-a0d8d899ca04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304976} {:answer/id #uuid "4bf3ff45-c8a5-5493-b4a8-f5463a6bd2ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304977} {:answer/id #uuid "2f8a3db6-c440-5bf6-ae84-805d076130e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-30 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304978} {:answer/id #uuid "be25d5a3-63a1-589a-8d12-f5b0c73b490f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304979} {:answer/id #uuid "72f8e646-aefa-573f-bb99-790398bb6c3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304980}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd95bf8e-829a-55b9-89e9-a0d8d899ca04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304976} :answer-field/id #uuid "4bdbcdf0-b3ed-5eda-9596-47f9c1d7f98d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304975}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8c43eaff-6e8a-54f3-9041-509e363b9890" :question/math-academy-id "q-129615" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & {x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-1 \\\\  & -{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=7 \\\\  & 2{x}_{3}=4\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The third equation states that \n\n$$\n2{x}_{3}=4\\,⟹\\,{x}_{3}=2.\n$$\n\n Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-{x}_{2}+3(2)=7\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=6-7=-1.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{3}=2$ and ${x}_{2}=-1$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+5(-1)+(2)=-1\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-1+5-2=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is \n${x}_{1}=2$, ${x}_{2}=-1$, and ${x}_{3}=2.$  In vector form, the solution can be written as $[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097096 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b8f8937b-de15-5d4c-aa77-1d45595fc7af" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations Using Back Substitution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87efb99c-9053-58b3-bc51-b3013a122463" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{3}{2}, 2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094983} {:answer/id #uuid "d65e0883-44ce-5600-90ae-2b83968ff1c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨ - \\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{1}{2}, 2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094984} {:answer/id #uuid "e4321a7d-f04a-5dcd-a079-753fa11c77a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{5}{2}, 1, \\frac{5}{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094985} {:answer/id #uuid "5e878129-c3d2-572d-ae30-8cba39487f93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{2}, 2,-\\frac{3}{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094986} {:answer/id #uuid "6524bc28-ee23-5c21-be46-4499e7c20a00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{5}{2}, \\frac{5}{2}, 2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094987}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6524bc28-ee23-5c21-be46-4499e7c20a00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{5}{2}, \\frac{5}{2}, 2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094987} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3e5efbf-3c10-5e91-b46f-c7af4ec2de09" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094982}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2386cda0-88d9-5e63-84f4-46ef34183090" :question/math-academy-id "q-20418" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=3 \\\\  & {x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & {x}_{3}=2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The third equation states that ${x}_{3}=2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}-(2)=\\frac{1}{2}\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2}+2=\\frac{5}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{2}=\\frac{5}{2}$ and ${x}_{3}=2$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+(\\frac{5}{2})-(2)=3\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=3+2-\\frac{5}{2}=\\frac{5}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is ${x}_{1}=\\frac{5}{2}$, ${x}_{2}=\\frac{5}{2}$, and ${x}_{3}=2.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨\\frac{5}{2},\\frac{5}{2},2⟩.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304981 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de05090a-2461-514a-971d-b83c7cea124e" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations Using Back Substitution Given an Augmented Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d16dbda-c032-5ce8-8554-7eac7c838f67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,-1,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304983} {:answer/id #uuid "f6332ea8-844f-595d-be47-10b7cb24f099" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-5,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304984} {:answer/id #uuid "c8ad4e40-3a26-5233-b388-78a94b23c49a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,-4,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304985} {:answer/id #uuid "31f4a5fb-1bd9-54b3-86c2-992fe4b95bee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-8,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304986} {:answer/id #uuid "e59803c6-4f0d-5506-b243-acceca6606a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,-3,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304987}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f6332ea8-844f-595d-be47-10b7cb24f099" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-5,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304984} :answer-field/id #uuid "e24c0b56-c2df-59fc-a3eb-0520a82a63d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304982}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8ab8c60d-5430-57fc-a283-bc3692f237cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-72972" :question/problem "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x$, $y$, and $z.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+2y+z=-8 \\\\  & y+2z=-1 \\\\  & z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that $z=2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+2(2)=-1\\,⟹\\,y=-1-4=-5.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=2$ and $y=-5$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+2(-5)+(2)=-8\\,⟹\\,x=-8+10-2=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=0$, $y=-5$, and $z=2.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨0,-5,2⟩.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304988 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de05090a-2461-514a-971d-b83c7cea124e" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations Using Back Substitution Given an Augmented Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a8db00c-9bdd-558f-a610-eb8e0db31f3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304990} {:answer/id #uuid "45fc48ab-b908-5066-96ed-b0529967aa5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304991} {:answer/id #uuid "b1e02ac5-b200-510c-b992-56f824058b21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304992} {:answer/id #uuid "0772fc5c-e315-5830-8cc4-de47bad2cd1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304993} {:answer/id #uuid "d3af7ab8-ef27-570c-9735-3b7c2ddc6612" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304994}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3af7ab8-ef27-570c-9735-3b7c2ddc6612" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304994} :answer-field/id #uuid "9050c533-c1a6-5967-b42d-a8a454ee3269" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304989}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cadceb90-b589-55eb-81c2-7bb7de4f1a06" :question/math-academy-id "q-72978" :question/problem "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say,  ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}=-3 \\\\  & {x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=-4 \\\\  & {x}_{3}=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that  ${x}_{3}=-1.$ Substituting this into the second equation,  we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+3(-1)=-4\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-4+3=-1.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{3}=-1$ and ${x}_{2}=-1$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+(-1)+4(-1)=-3\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-3+1+4=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is ${x}_{1}=2$, ${x}_{2}=-1$, and ${x}_{3}=-1.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as\n$[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304995 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "52e51c9a-6bce-5ea6-a9fe-febb09f8754d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations Given an Augmented Matrix Containing Non-Unit Leading Entries"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b02f1c1-08b2-510e-8e1f-64f312f89d07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,4,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304997} {:answer/id #uuid "37fabebe-4aac-5c89-aa6c-173d855f3d37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,-3,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304998} {:answer/id #uuid "499125a6-45eb-51c6-a59d-4a00033ac533" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,-3,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304999} {:answer/id #uuid "1d616cc2-cfac-5774-a7cc-cab8e41e4940" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,-4,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305000} {:answer/id #uuid "0b6f5e3b-de33-5b71-aefa-ddead7c1603a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,3,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305001}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37fabebe-4aac-5c89-aa6c-173d855f3d37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,-3,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304998} :answer-field/id #uuid "614a3b60-e86f-5567-923f-e609ab89f646" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304996}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3ee944c9-4b43-5da0-ab41-c5200c36245b" :question/math-academy-id "q-72980" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 2x+y-z=2 \\\\  & y+3z=6 \\\\  & -z=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The third equation states that\n\n$$\n-z=-3\\,⟹\\,z=3.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+3(3)=6\\,⟹\\,y=6-9=-3.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=3$ and $y=-3$ into the first equation to get \n\n$$\n2x+(-3)-(3)=2\\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{1}{2}(2+3+3)=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=4$, $y=-3$ and $z=3.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨4,-3,3⟩.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305002 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "52e51c9a-6bce-5ea6-a9fe-febb09f8754d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations Given an Augmented Matrix Containing Non-Unit Leading Entries"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f457b3a-0152-50e2-8a41-4a037ce038ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305004} {:answer/id #uuid "9cc151f6-e1ea-522c-bf33-e362ba3eb24f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305005} {:answer/id #uuid "08a6391a-012b-5b5c-9204-ac55f6ae0c02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305006} {:answer/id #uuid "db28743f-692a-54d1-ab07-b7d5c103e0a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305007} {:answer/id #uuid "f5e47b5b-ca91-593c-b2dd-65beb434984b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305008}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db28743f-692a-54d1-ab07-b7d5c103e0a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305007} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4583fae-dac3-5c1c-ae90-1949b18bda67" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305003}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c67fc178-cf1a-54db-8b4d-208b21f2bc23" :question/math-academy-id "q-72981" :question/problem "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix: \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x$, $y$, and $z.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations: \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+z=2 \\\\  & 3y+2z=-1 \\\\  & -z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that\n\n$$\n-z=2\\,⟹\\,z=-2.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n3y+2(-2)=-1\\,⟹\\,y=\\frac{1}{3}(-1+4)=1.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=-2$ and $y=1$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+(-2)=2\\,⟹\\,x=2+2=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=4$, $y=1$, and $z=-2.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as \n$[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$"}]}
